@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Medium Parametric Diagram with Ohm's law and power constraints sharing bound parameters, value properties bound to parameter ports.
'   usecase:      Teach 2-3 constraint blocks sharing bound parameters and value properties bound to parameter ports.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       electrical
' ============================================================================
title Example Parametric - Medium Circuit Equations

note top of "OhmsLaw"
  PARAMETRIC DIAGRAM NOTE:
  All edges are BINDING CONNECTORS (==) =
  equality constraints. No flow occurs.
  Two constraint blocks sharing a bound
  parameter form a coupled equation set.
end note

class "OhmsLaw" <<constraint>> {
  { V = I * R }
}

class "PowerLaw" <<constraint>> {
  { P = V * I }
}

class "EnergyCost" <<constraint>> {
  { cost = P * rate * t }
}

package "Binding context (inside a ResistorCircuit block)" {
  object "vVal : Voltage" as vVal
  object "iVal : Current" as iVal
  object "rVal : Resistance" as rVal
  object "pVal : Power" as pVal

  class "OhmsLawInst" as "ohm : OhmsLaw" <<constraint>> { }
  class "PowerLawInst" as "pow : PowerLaw" <<constraint>> { }
  class "EnergyCostInst" as "ec : EnergyCost" <<constraint>> { }

  object "rateVal : CostPerEnergy" as rateVal
  object "tVal : Duration" as tVal
  object "costVal : Currency" as costVal
}

vVal == ohm
iVal == ohm
rVal == ohm

vVal == pow
iVal == pow
pVal == pow

pVal == ec
rateVal == ec
tVal == ec
costVal == ec

note right of pow
  P (in PowerLaw) and V,I are bound to the
  SAME value properties as Ohm's law, so
  V couples the two constraint blocks:
  both equations must hold simultaneously.
end note

@enduml
